message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Aging-like BAC sectors when coupling travels through barrier-limited desmoplastic edges"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Do aging-like Bounded Adaptive Coherence sectors that appear under lumped
  coupling still appear when the same subsystem couples only through
  barrier-limited desmoplastic edges, or does the barrier schedule carve a
  different sector map? The barrier schedule carves a different map when the
  stalled fractions differ by sector. The five-index weight matrix of Thesis
  #25 is read by that deposit's sector classifier. Under the barrier reading
  each edge is a series pair in the sense of Thesis #21, and the Laplacian
  sees only the series flux. A uniform stalled fraction keeps global decay
  aging-like. Assigning the transport-limited stalled fraction 0.705882 to
  one sector and the shedding-limited fraction 0.264706 to the other classes
  that same path neither, and the aging-like sets on the 169-node rate plane
  are disjoint. Co-decay of conductance with shedding restores the lumped
  map. No rejuvenation claim. Not a medical device. No document DOI.
keywords:
  - bounded adaptive coherence
  - sector classifier
  - grounded Laplacian
  - desmoplastic conductance
  - series flux
  - stalled fraction
  - barrier schedule
  - research-only
